  "details": "SDK:\nVRCSDK3-WORLD-2021.02.23.11.40_Public\n\nDescription:\nWhen attempting to place down a node from the 'UnityEngine.ParticleSystem.Particle[]' type, it messes up the graph.\nAfter reloading the aforementioned graph, nearly all of the nodes become invisible, yet their 'noodles' are retained.\nI'd also like to note that if you create a 'Particle[]' variable and try to change the contents, it yeilds a warning which mentions that the object type of the array is 'UnityEngine.ParticleSystem+Particle'. (Could this be part of the issue?)\nIt is possible to unhide some of the nodes if you're selecting random things inside the graph, but this effort is ultimately undone when the graph is reloaded once again.\n\nReplication:\n1. Create a new Udon graph. (So that nothing's messed up elsewhere.)\n2. Search for the type 'Particle[]'.\n3. Add any node from within this type. (Note that the newly added node is invisible.)\n4. Reload graph and notice how alot of the nodes now appear to be invisible. (Optional.)\n\nPictures:\na) Warning recieved when trying to edit a 'Particle[]' variable.\nb) Graph after adding a 'Particle[]' node to it and reloading it.",
